  Parameters: %{"background_tasks" => [], "cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/phx-new-generator", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "6bc4851f-f735-4590-bb1c-c660619b4019", "hook_event_name" => "Stop", "last_assistant_message" => "Both auth fixes are in (`8806ad88`), 269 tests green.\n\n**On the migration — I want to correct one premise before anyone acts on it.** The harness reports to `http://localhost:4000`, not dev.codemyspec.com. `just harness` defaults `server=\"http://localhost:4000\"`, and `/health` confirms it. So the \"1 story\" side is `code_my_spec_dev` (Postgres), and the 99 stories are in `cli.db` (SQLite). That matters because migrating toward the wrong destination would be worse than not migrating.\n\nThe `dev_cli.exs` config you're thinking of *does* say dev.codemyspec.com — but that's `harness_default_server_url`, the fallback used only when `CMS_SERVER_URL` and `:harness_server_url` say nothing. The justfile passes an explicit server, so the default never applies.\n\nSo the real question is which of three destinations is canonical — `cli.db`, `code_my_spec_dev`, or dev.codemyspec.com — and that's your call, not something I should infer. The other agent's framing (\"re-migrate to the server\") is right in shape; I'd just want to know which server before moving 99 stories anywhere.\n\n**What I'd want to check before any migration**, since it decides whether this is a copy or a merge: whether those 99 stories carry the same ids as the 1 in Postgres, and whether 727 exists in `cli.db` too. If ids collide, it's a merge with a conflict policy; if they're disjoint, it's a copy.\n\nSay which destination is canonical and I'll work out the actual shape of it. I'd rather not guess at that one — it's the kind of thing that looks fine until a week of story work quietly disappears.", "permission_mode" => "auto", "prompt_id" => "6689c90f-0679-471b-a1f0-f9de9c127399", "session_crons" => [], "session_id" =