[debug] Processing with CmsHarness.Web.HooksController.handle/2
  Parameters: %{"background_tasks" => [], "cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/phx-new-generator", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "6bc4851f-f735-4590-bb1c-c660619b4019", "hook_event_name" => "Stop", "last_assistant_message" => "No — and I should have said what I was doing rather than let it look like that.\n\n**I found the actual cause of the empty requirement state.** It isn't going to repopulate, so their instinct to wait would have burned time. `export_story` carries title, story, description and status — it never carried `component_id`. In the source 97 of 99 stories have a component; the destination has zero. Requirements are computed per story×component, so everything reports 0/0.\n\n**Fixed:** export now carries `component_module_name` rather than the id, because components are file projections — each deployment derives its own, so the ids differ but the module name is the natural key both sides already enforce. Import resolves it, and leaves a story unlinked if that component doesn't exist here rather than inventing one.\n\n**Also fixed a boundary violation I'd introduced** — `cms.harness.onboard` was `classify_to: CodeMySpec` while using `CmsHarness` modules, and the dependency only runs the other way. That one matters beyond tidiness: the analyzer treats any compiler problem as grounds to skip exunit, credo and spex entirely, so a single misclassified line was suppressing every other check and serving stale results.\n\nThe spex fumbling was me trying to verify the migration fix against its own 991 spex and getting `--pattern` wrong twice. Not worth more time — the 4 migration unit tests pass and compile is clean.\n\n**What's still open is the part that unblocks them:** the code fix only helps *future* imports, because `put_stories` skips stories whose title already exists. The 100 stories already in `code_my_spec_dev` are still unlinked. That needs a backfill by module name — same matching logic, applied to what's already there.\n\nWant me to run that now? It's the difference between the graph working for them and not. Their sigmajs point is separate and I haven't touched it.", "permission_mode" => "auto", "prompt_id" => "4de804e1-b724-464b-a4ca-1c4707223a09", "session_crons" => [], "session_id" => "80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37", "stop_hook_active" => false, "transcript_path" => "/Users/johndavenport/.claude/projects/-Users-johndavenport-Documents-github-code-my-spec--claude-worktrees-phx-new-generator/80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37.jsonl"}
