[debug] Processing with CmsHarness.Web.HooksController.handle/2
  Parameters: %{"background_tasks" => [], "cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/phx-new-generator", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "6bc4851f-f735-4590-bb1c-c660619b4019", "hook_event_name" => "Stop", "last_assistant_message" => "Done — `main` at `21669e2c`.\n\n**Tell them not to wait: it was never going to repopulate.** Their reasoning was sound (requirements *are* computed from files and problems, and those repopulate fine — 4,491 / 4,223 / 2,070 files per harness, 864 components, 1,183 problems). But requirements are computed per story **and component**, and the migration never carried `component_id`. Every story arrived unlinked, so the graph had nothing to compute against.\n\n**Fixed both halves.** The exporter now carries `component_module_name` — by name, not id, because components are file projections and each deployment derives its own set, so ids differ while the module name is the natural key both sides already enforce. And I backfilled what was already there, since `put_stories` skips existing titles: **84 of 100 stories are now linked**.\n\nThe remaining 16: 9 point at components this deployment doesn't have yet (`AgentProgressLive`, `AppLive`, `IntakeLive`, `IssuesLive`, `PersonasLive`, `TaskQueueLive` among them), and 7 never had one in the source. The 9 will link on a rescan if those components appear — worth a second backfill then. So `get_next_requirement` is trustworthy for the 84, and blind to the rest.\n\nTwo things I fixed on the way that matter beyond this:\n\n`cms.harness.onboard` was `classify_to: CodeMySpec` while using `CmsHarness` modules. The analyzer treats *any* compiler problem as grounds to skip exunit, credo and spex entirely — so one misclassified line was suppressing every other check and serving previous results as current. That's worth knowing generally: a stray compiler warning silently disables the whole gate.\n\nAnd `put_rules`/`put_criteria` were three levels deep and failing the file's credo check. Flattened without behaviour change; 4 migration tests and 142 harness tests green.\n\n**Still untouched: the sigmajs graph.** Their point is that the rendering lives in `code_my_spec_local_web` and needs to move into `CodeMySpecWeb` for the graph to render on the cloud — that's the portable-UI migration, and it's a separate piece of work I haven't started.", "permission_mode" => "auto", "prompt_id" => "22082e4a-e3e2-45c9-812d-d39cd80412db", "session_crons" => [], "session_id" => "80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37", "stop_hook_active" => false, "transcript_path" => "/Users/johndavenport/.claude/projects/-Users-johndavenport-Documents-github-code-my-spec--claude-worktrees-phx-new-generator/80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37.jsonl"}
