  Parameters: %{"cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/phx-new-generator", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "6bc4851f-f735-4590-bb1c-c660619b4019", "hook_event_name" => "PreToolUse", "permission_mode" => "auto", "prompt_id" => "22082e4a-e3e2-45c9-812d-d39cd80412db", "session_id" => "80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37", "tool_input" => %{"content" => "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 2,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"create_issue\",\n    \"arguments\": {\n      \"scope\": \"framework\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"title\": \"Stop hook blocks on credo problems the analyzer already cleared, at stale line numbers\",\n      \"source_path\": \"lib/code_my_spec/migration.ex\",\n      \"description\": \"The stop hook has blocked three consecutive stops on two credo findings that no longer exist, and it labels them `stale` while also asserting `Analysis is running now`. Neither is true.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\nReported by the hook:\\n\\n    credo (2) - stale:\\n      - lib/code_my_spec/migration.ex:270 - Function body is nested too deep\\n      - lib/code_my_spec/migration.ex:319 - Function body is nested too deep\\n\\nStored rows, however, are at lines 236 and 285 - the positions before the file was edited - so the hook is rendering stored problems against a file that has moved underneath them. Running the analyzer directly:\\n\\n    MIX_ENV=test mix credo lib/code_my_spec/migration.ex --strict\\n    => 43 mods/funs, found no issues.\\n\\nThe nesting was flattened in c3dc4c32; both functions are now two deep.\\n\\n## Two distinct defects\\n\\n**1. The blocking set contains `info` severity.** These rows are `severity=info` in the problems table, and the same hook message separately reports `credo: 558 infos (advisory)`. So identical severity is presented as both blocking and advisory in one message. Probably the same root cause as issue 7bee1703.\\n\\n**2. `Analysis is running now` is asserted without a run.** server.log shows the last credo run finishing at 18:18:03 and reconciling, 75 minutes before the most recent stop. Nothing was enqueued after it. The message tells the agent to stop again and let a rerun replace the findings, but no rerun is coming, so the instruction produces an unbounded stop loop.\\n\\n## Why it matters\\n\\nThe hook's own guidance says to report rather than edit around it, which is right - but an agent that follows the stale-then-retry instruction never terminates, and one that does not follow it edits code that is already correct. On this occasion I refactored two pre-existing functions I had not touched, purely to clear a block that was reporting positions from a previous version of the file.\\n\\n## Suggested fix\\n\\nExclude `info` from the blocking set so it matches the advisory count, and only claim analysis is running when a run is actually enqueued - otherwise say the results are stale and name when they were produced.\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n", "file_path" => "/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-johndavenport-Documents-github-code-my-spec--claude-worktrees-phx-new-generator/80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37/scratchpad/issue.json"}, "tool_name" => "Write", "tool_use_id" => "toolu_01PSKKHQocytrnBjw4URopCB", "transcript_path" => "/Users/johndavenport/.claude/projects/-Users-johndavenport-Documents-github-code-my-spec--claude-worktrees-phx-new-generator/80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37.jsonl"}
