  Parameters: %{"background_tasks" => [], "cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/phx-new-generator", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "6bc4851f-f735-4590-bb1c-c660619b4019", "hook_event_name" => "Stop", "last_assistant_message" => "Filed as `a1e3d3f1`, framework scope.\n\n**It's not the analyzer failing — it's the hook reporting.** Two separate defects, with evidence:\n\nThe stored rows are at lines **236 and 285**, the positions *before* I edited the file; the hook renders them as 270 and 319. Running credo directly gives `43 mods/funs, found no issues`. So it's rendering stored problems against a file that has moved underneath them.\n\nBoth rows are **`severity=info`** — and the same message separately reports \"credo: 558 infos (advisory)\". Identical severity, presented as blocking in one line and advisory in the next. That's almost certainly the same root cause as the already-open `7bee1703`.\n\nAnd \"Analysis is running now\" isn't true. `server.log` shows credo last finishing at **18:18:03** and reconciling; nothing has been enqueued in the 75 minutes since. So \"stop again and let the rerun replace these\" describes a rerun that isn't coming — which makes the instruction a non-terminating loop for any agent that follows it.\n\nWorth naming the cost: I refactored `put_rules` and `put_criteria` — two pre-existing functions I hadn't touched — purely to clear a block that was reporting stale positions. The refactor is fine and committed, but I shouldn't have needed to do it, and a less suspicious agent would have kept editing correct code indefinitely.\n\nSuggested fix is in the issue: exclude `info` from the blocking set so it agrees with the advisory count, and only claim analysis is running when something is actually enqueued — otherwise say the results are stale and when they were produced.\n\nEverything is committed and pushed at `21669e2c`.", "permission_mode" => "auto", "prompt_id" => "22082e4a-e3e