[debug] Processing with CmsHarness.Web.HooksController.handle/2
  Parameters: %{"background_tasks" => [], "cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/phx-new-generator", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "6bc4851f-f735-4590-bb1c-c660619b4019", "hook_event_name" => "Stop", "last_assistant_message" => "Dismissed. The headline claim was reporter error — I concluded the hook was lying about analysis running when the log went quiet, without asking why it went quiet. A restart drops the queue and the ledger, so there was nothing to explain.\n\nWhat survives is narrower and already filed: the two blocking rows were `severity=info` while the same message called 558 infos advisory. That's `7bee1703`, and a second issue for it is noise. I carried one detail into the dismissal worth having when that gets worked — the rows rendered at lines 270/319 while stored at 236/285, so a stale finding that also points at the wrong line is much harder to recognise as stale.\n\nThat's the second time today I've filed something on incomplete evidence and had to retract, which is a pattern worth me watching rather than shrugging off.\n\nThe work itself stands, all pushed at `21669e2c`:\n\n- **Migration carries story→component links** — the real cause of 0/0 requirement state, since requirements compute per story *and* component. 84 of 100 stories backfilled; 9 await components this deployment doesn't have yet, 7 never had one.\n- **Two CLI migrations unblocked** — `ALTER COLUMN` isn't SQLite, and because the migrator is a supervised child, that was a CLI that wouldn't boot at all for anyone on a database older than `20260801`.\n- **Auth messages fixed** — `/app/auth` instead of the 404, and the project-scoped-deploy-key case no longer told to sign in again in a loop it can't exit.\n- **Boundary fix on `cms.harness.onboard`** — worth repeating because it's a trap: any compiler problem makes the analyzer skip exunit, credo and spex entirely and serve previous results as current.\n\nStill open and untouched: the sigmajs graph move from `code_my_spec_local_web` into `CodeMySpecWeb`.", "permission_mode" => "auto", "prompt_id" => "27bbe924-2967-40f5-bcec-c9f954997bba", "session_crons" => [], "session_id" => "80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37", "stop_hook_active" => false, "transcript_path" => "/Users/johndavenport/.claude/projects/-Users-johndavenport-Documents-github-code-my-spec--claude-worktrees-phx-new-generator/80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37.jsonl"}
