[debug] Processing with CmsHarness.Web.HooksController.handle/2
  Parameters: %{"cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/phx-new-generator", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "6bc4851f-f735-4590-bb1c-c660619b4019", "hook_event_name" => "PreToolUse", "permission_mode" => "auto", "prompt_id" => "a0ba002e-cead-431e-9d54-ce5a335f64e4", "session_id" => "80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37", "tool_input" => %{"command" => "elixir -S mix format lib/cms_harness/project/channel_client.ex test/cms_harness/channel_client_transport_test.exs 2>&1|tail -1; git add lib/cms_harness/project/channel_client.ex test/cms_harness/channel_client_transport_test.exs && git commit -q -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nReconnect after a disconnect even when the join was refused\n\nhandle_disconnect/2 returned without arming a timer if `refused` was set,\nso a refusal followed by a socket drop was permanent. The refusal path\nreschedules; a socket that then dropped landed here and scheduled\nnothing, and the subtree sat refusing every hook with \"the server is\nanswering but this harness cannot hold a socket to it\" until the process\nwas restarted.\n\nSeen today: two subtrees in one harness met the same server restart and\nonly the one that had never been refused came back. The moduledoc already\ndescribed this as fixed — the earlier fix covered `refused/2` and missed\nthis path, and the comment there even says the flag \"no longer gates the\nreconnect\", which was true of one caller out of two.\n\nNothing about a refusal makes reconnecting wrong. It means another\nprocess holds `_build`, which it releases when it exits, so waiting and\nretrying is the whole correct response.\n\nThe test that guarded this passed with the bug present. It drove refuse/1\neight times, each arming a rejoin timer — the first at 1000ms — and\ndrained for 50ms, so the timers were still pending rather than drained\nand the assertion was satisfied about a second later by a refusal's own\ntimer. It now sets `refused` directly and asserts the fixture arms\nnothing, so only handle_disconnect/2 can satisfy it. Verified failing\nagainst the previous implementation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JPoSfcCJqSqG8iGY9nfyfL\nEOF\n)\" && git log --oneline -1", "description" => "Commit the self-healing fix"}, "tool_name" => "Bash", "tool_use_id" => "toolu_01EmSCnkKhUzwtvxNE7VaQ3n", "transcript_path" => "/Users/johndavenport/.claude/projects/-Users-johndavenport-Documents-github-code-my-spec--claude-worktrees-phx-new-generator/80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37.jsonl"}
