  Parameters: %{"background_tasks" => [], "cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/phx-new-generator", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "6bc4851f-f735-4590-bb1c-c660619b4019", "hook_event_name" => "Stop", "last_assistant_message" => "Fixed properly — `main` at `4b799405`.\n\n**It genuinely wasn't self-healing, and now it is.** `handle_disconnect/2` returned without arming a reconnect timer whenever `refused` was set. So a refusal followed by a socket drop was permanent: the refusal path reschedules, but a socket that *then* dropped landed in the disconnect handler and scheduled nothing. That's precisely why two subtrees in one harness met your server restart and only the one that had never been refused came back.\n\nNothing about a refusal makes reconnecting wrong — it means another process holds `_build`, which it releases when it exits, so waiting and retrying is the whole correct response.\n\n**Two things about this are worth more than the fix itself.**\n\nThe moduledoc already claimed this was fixed, including the line \"it no longer gates the reconnect\" — which was true of one caller out of two. My earlier fix covered `refused/2` and missed the disconnect path, and the documentation went ahead of the implementation.\n\nAnd **the test guarding it passed with the bug present**. It drove `refuse/1` eight times, each arming a rejoin timer with the first at 1000ms, then drained for 50ms — so those timers were still pending rather than drained, and the assertion was satisfied a second later by a refusal's own timer, not by the code under test. I rewrote it to set `refused` directly, assert the fixture arms nothing, and only then call the handler. I verified it fails against the previous implementation before restoring the fix, which is the step that turns \"passes\" into \"means something.\"\n\nThat combination — a green test, a moduledoc describing the fix, and the bug still in the code — is how this survived. Worth remembering when the next thing looks covered.", "permission_mode" => "auto", "prompt_id" => "a0ba002e-cead-431e-9d54-ce5a335f64e4", "session_crons" => [], "session_id" => "80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37", "stop_hook_active" => false, "transcript_path" => "/Users/johndavenport/.claude/projects/-Users-johndavenport-Documents-github-code-my-spec--claude-worktrees-phx-new-generator/80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37.jsonl"}
