[debug] Processing with CmsHarness.Web.HooksController.handle/2
  Parameters: %{"cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/intake-on-home", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "d1c8f8f5-13e5-4827-865e-55a081f988a6", "hook_event_name" => "PreToolUse", "permission_mode" => "auto", "prompt_id" => "a5f861fc-8989-48ed-8aeb-001fcc86a060", "session_id" => "9703aaca-90cf-4469-8202-6146afe86064", "tool_input" => %{"command" => "cd /Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/intake-on-home\ngit commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nRegister SigmaGraph where the graphs actually render\n\nrequirements_live and architecture_live moved to CodeMySpecWeb, but the hook\nthey use stayed behind in local_app.js. The cloud app loads app.js, which\nregistered only StripePaymentElement and Copy — so every graph raised\n\"unknown hook found for SigmaGraph\" and drew nothing.\n\nThe hook and its four theme helpers move to assets/js/sigma_graph.js, which\nboth bundles import. Nothing about the hook changed.\n\ngraphology and sigma now come through esbuild alongside it, the way Sortable\nalready does. Loading them from priv/static was only ever going to work for\nthe local app: that path is checked in, while the cloud's priv/static/assets\nis gitignored build output, so a copy placed there would be correct locally\nand absent in production. Bundling is one path that survives a deploy.\n\nThe local root layout no longer loads them separately — they are in its\nbundle now, and it was fetching them twice.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TKK8AVqBPeeiV4LoTFkTRu\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1", "description" => "Commit the fix", "timeout" => 300000}, "tool_name" => "Bash", "tool_use_id" => "toolu_01QzTFeHULoKcqB38tfSK2XD", "transcript_path" => "/Users/johndavenport/.claude/projects/-Users-johndavenport-Documents-github-code-my-spec/9703aaca-90cf-4469-8202-6146afe86064.jsonl"}
