  Parameters: %{"background_tasks" => [], "cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/phx-new-generator", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "6bc4851f-f735-4590-bb1c-c660619b4019", "hook_event_name" => "Stop", "last_assistant_message" => "This is worse than a renumbering, and it lands on the story we've spent all day on.\n\n| id | in `cli.db` (`:4003`) | in `code_my_spec_dev` (`:4004`) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **727** | Engineer trusts QA pass claims as audit-grade events | **Agents working the same project do not collide** |\n| **875** | *(nothing)* | Guided intake takes a visitor from an idea to a running app |\n| **990** | Guided intake takes a visitor from an idea to a running app | *(nothing)* |\n| **1000** | A pane that shows my app… | *(it's 885 here)* |\n\nSo \"story 727\" names two different stories depending on which system you ask, and both answers are valid. Guided intake is 990 in one and 875 in the other. The ranges overlap (62–1001 vs 727–886), so you don't get a clean \"not found\" to warn you — you get a confident wrong answer.\n\n**And there's no way to translate.** The payload carries `local_id`, but the importer only uses it to wire up references within the transaction and never persists it. The sole correspondence between the two systems is story *title*, which is also what `put_stories` dedupes on. Nothing records that destination 885 came from source 1000.\n\n**This will recur on the prod migration**, which is the thing you said you want to move on. Same code, same remapping, and prod already has its own stories, so the collisions will be different but no less confident.\n\nThe fix I'd suggest is small and belongs in the migration: persist the source id on the destination row — a `migrated_from_id` column, or in existing metadata if there's a suitable field. That makes translation mechanical, makes a re-run idempotent on something better than title, and makes \"which 727?\" answerable.\n\nI'd want your call before adding a column, since it's schema on both deployments. Want me to do it, or is title-matching good enough given the two systems aren't meant to coexist for long?", "permission_mode" => "auto", "prompt_id" => "b972f327-510b-40ba-b372-d740d67d9d5b", "session_crons" => [], "session_id" => "80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37", "stop_hook_active" => false, "transcript_path" => "/Users/johndavenport/.claude/projects/-Users-johndavenport-Documents-github-code-my-spec--claude-worktrees-phx-new-generator/80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37.jsonl"}
