[debug] Processing with CmsHarness.Web.HooksController.handle/2
  Parameters: %{"background_tasks" => [], "cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/intake-on-home", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "d1c8f8f5-13e5-4827-865e-55a081f988a6", "hook_event_name" => "Stop", "last_assistant_message" => "On main — `da0b52ae → 9290ecde`, fast-forward, verified against origin.\n\n**The cause:** `requirements_live` and `architecture_live` moved to `CodeMySpecWeb`, but their hook stayed behind in `local_app.js`. The cloud app loads `app.js`, which registered only `StripePaymentElement` and `Copy` — so both graph pages raised *\"unknown hook found for SigmaGraph\"* and drew nothing.\n\n**The fix:** the hook and its four theme helpers moved to `assets/js/sigma_graph.js`, imported by both bundles. The hook's code is unchanged.\n\n**One thing that changed shape mid-fix.** My first attempt copied `graphology`/`sigma` into `priv/static/assets/js/` and added script tags to the cloud layout. That would have worked locally and silently failed in production — `.gitignore:30` excludes `/priv/static/assets/`, so those files would never have been committed. I caught it on `git status` showing nothing to stage. They now come through esbuild alongside the hook, the way `Sortable` already does, which is one path that survives a deploy. As a side effect the local layout stopped fetching them twice.\n\n**Verified rather than assumed:** both bundles rebuild clean and contain `SigmaGraph` and the `window.graphology` assignment; `mix compile` is clean; and the hook is present in `origin/main`.\n\nTwo notes:\n\nThe rebase conflicted on 3,528 lines of minified `local_app.js`. I regenerated it from source rather than hand-merging. Left as-is per your call — it is Phoenix's default posture — but worth knowing the underlying reason is that `assets.build`/`assets.deploy` only name the `code_my_spec` profile, never `code_my_spec_local`. That's why that one bundle must be tracked.\n\nAnd I couldn't confirm this in a browser: the `:4000` dev server runs from the **main** checkout, not this worktree, so it still serves the old bundle. Once it picks up main, the graphs should render. If you want, load `/app/architecture` after it restarts and confirm the console is quiet — that's the last unverified step.", "permission_mode" => "auto", "prompt_id" => "5085579c-7279-452c-a5dd-adf1c23ae768", "session_crons" => [], "session_id" => "9703aaca-90cf-4469-8202-6146afe86064", "stop_hook_active" => false, "transcript_path" => "/Users/johndavenport/.claude/projects/-Users-johndavenport-Documents-github-code-my-spec/9703aaca-90cf-4469-8202-6146afe86064.jsonl"}
