[debug] Processing with CmsHarness.Web.HooksController.handle/2
  Parameters: %{"cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/phx-new-generator", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "6bc4851f-f735-4590-bb1c-c660619b4019", "hook_event_name" => "PreToolUse", "permission_mode" => "auto", "prompt_id" => "39150913-9d7c-48ec-b910-e10e2210de14", "session_id" => "80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37", "tool_input" => %{"command" => "git commit -q -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nRecord which story a migrated story was, on the source\n\nStory ids are per-deployment sequences, so migrating renumbers everything\n— and the ranges overlap, which is what makes it dangerous rather than\nmerely inconvenient. After migrating this project, 727 named \"Agents\nworking the same project do not collide\" on the server and \"Engineer\ntrusts QA pass claims as audit-grade events\" on the harness. Guided\nintake was 990 on one side and 875 on the other. Nothing errors: both\nsides answer confidently and disagree, and an agent told \"use story_id\n1000\" acts on a different story.\n\nNothing could translate. The payload carried local_id to wire up\nreferences inside the import transaction and then discarded it, leaving\ntitle as the only correspondence.\n\nSo the source id travels and is stored. A second run now recognises its\nown rows by an id the source owns rather than by a string a human edits —\nretitling a story upstream used to make it a second story here.\n\nTitle stays as a fallback, but only for a row that cannot say where it\ncame from. A row naming a *different* source story is a different story\nthat happens to share a title, and matching it merged two of Sam's\nstories into whichever arrived first while reporting both as migrated.\nNow it falls through to the insert, where the destination's unique title\nindex refuses it and the import rolls back — loud and recoverable rather\nthan quiet and lossy.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JPoSfcCJqSqG8iGY9nfyfL\nEOF\n)\" && git log --oneline -1", "description" => "Commit the migration identity fix"}, "tool_name" => "Bash", "tool_use_id" => "toolu_01PNZNgKR7ySCKHFtvezYp7e", "transcript_path" => "/Users/johndavenport/.claude/projects/-Users-johndavenport-Documents-github-code-my-spec--claude-worktrees-phx-new-generator/80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37.jsonl"}
