[debug] Processing with CmsHarness.Web.HooksController.handle/2
  Parameters: %{"background_tasks" => [], "cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/intake-on-home", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "d1c8f8f5-13e5-4827-865e-55a081f988a6", "hook_event_name" => "Stop", "last_assistant_message" => "On main — `9290ecde → 8fc872ea`.\n\nYou were right and I should have done this the first time. The working code loaded these by script tag; I changed the mechanism instead of copying it. The gitignore problem was real, but it called for a *tracked directory*, not a different loading strategy.\n\n**What actually broke:** graphology survived bundling because it's a genuine UMD (`module.exports = …`). Sigma isn't a module at all — `var Sigma;(()=>{…})()` — so it only becomes a global under a script tag. Bundled, that `var` stayed module-scoped, the import yielded an empty object, and `new SigmaClass(...)` threw.\n\n**Now:** both apps load both libraries by script tag, exactly as the local app always did. The cloud serves them from `priv/static/vendor/` — tracked, and added to `static_paths` — rather than `priv/static/assets/`, which is esbuild's outdir and gitignored.\n\nBundle sizes returning to 386.7kb and 369.7kb confirm the libraries are out of the bundles again; the local one is byte-identical to what shipped before.\n\nThe local app is back to exactly its previous configuration — same files, same script tags. The only change there is that its hook now comes from the shared module.\n\nI've left a comment in `sigma_graph.js` naming the trap, since \"just bundle it like Sortable\" is the obvious-looking move that fails here.\n\nWhat I have **not** done is see a graph render. The `:4000` dev server runs from the main checkout, so it's still serving the old bundle. Once it picks up main, `/app/architecture` is the check — and given I broke this twice, I'd rather you confirm the console is clean than take my word for it.", "permission_mode" => "auto", "prompt_id" => "0a51891b-5e52-47a1-9