[debug] Processing with CmsHarness.Web.HooksController.handle/2
  Parameters: %{"background_tasks" => [], "cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/phx-new-generator", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "6bc4851f-f735-4590-bb1c-c660619b4019", "hook_event_name" => "Stop", "last_assistant_message" => "Done — `main` at `e4b7ac60`. The migration now preserves identity.\n\n**What changed:** stories carry `migrated_from_id`, so the renumbering is reversible. Migration on both Postgres and the SQLite mirror, unique per project where set. All 99 already-migrated stories backfilled by title — the one correspondence those rows had.\n\n**A second run now recognises its own work by an id the source owns**, not by a title a human edits. Retitling a story upstream used to create a duplicate on the next run.\n\n**And I found a worse bug than the one I set out to fix.** Title-matching didn't just fail on retitles — it *merged distinct stories*. Two source stories sharing a title matched the same destination row, and the importer counted both as migrated while only one existed. Title is now a fallback only for rows that can't say where they came from; a row naming a different source story falls through to the insert, where the unique title index refuses it and the whole import rolls back. Loud beats lossy.\n\nFour tests pin it, including the retitle case that was silently broken.\n\n**One correction to something I told you earlier.** I said the destination could collapse two same-titled stories into one row. That's wrong — `stories_title_project_id_index` already prevents it at the database. The real merge was happening a layer up, in the importer's title fallback, before the insert was ever attempted. Same outcome, different mechanism, and the fix is in the right place now.\n\n**For the prod migration**, this matters more than here: prod already has its own stories, so its id collisions will be different but equally confident. Worth running the same backfill against any project already migrated there — the script's in scratchpad and takes source DB and project id.", "permission_mode" => "auto", "prompt_id" => "39150913-9d7c-48ec-b910-e10e2210de14", "session_crons" => [], "session_id" => "80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37", "stop_hook_active" => false, "transcript_path" => "/Users/johndavenport/.claude/projects/-Users-johndavenport-Documents-github-code-my-spec--claude-worktrees-phx-new-generator/80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37.jsonl"}
