  Parameters: %{"background_tasks" => [], "cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/phx-new-generator", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "6bc4851f-f735-4590-bb1c-c660619b4019", "hook_event_name" => "Stop", "last_assistant_message" => "That explains all nine, and none of it is the migration's doing.\n\n**The links came over faithfully.** 84 of 93 landed, and not one points at the wrong component. The nine that didn't land reference components that genuinely don't exist at the destination, for two reasons:\n\n**The modules moved.** `CodeMySpecLocalWeb.AgentProgressLive` is now `CodeMySpecWeb.AgentProgressLive` — the file only exists under `code_my_spec_web`. Same for `CodeMySpecLocalWeb.Tasks.TaskQueueLive` → `CodeMySpecWeb.Tasks.TaskQueueLive`. That's the portable-UI migration, and `cli.db`'s component graph predates it.\n\n**The rest are namespace anchors.** The source links stories to `CodeMySpecWeb.AppLive`, `PersonasLive`, `IssuesLive`, `IntakeLive` — bare namespaces. The destination has only the real modules underneath: `AppLive.Overview`, `PersonasLive.Index`, `PersonasLive.Show`, `PersonasLive.FormComponent`, `IntakeLive.Plan`, `IntakeLive.Workspace`. The destination's ComponentSync doesn't create a component for a namespace with no module, which is the \"no fake contexts\" rule.\n\nSo `cli.db` holds nine stale links, and the destination correctly declines to invent components to satisfy them. A story pointed at `CodeMySpecWeb.AppLive` genuinely needs re-pointing at `AppLive.Overview` — that's a judgement about which module owns the story, not something a migration can infer. Guessing would produce exactly the fiction the importer refuses to create.\n\nTwo ways forward, and I'd take the first:\n\n**Let ArchitectureDesign handle them.** That's what `get_next_requirement` already asked for, and re-pointing nine stories at the right modules is precisely its job.\n\n**Or map the two moved ones mechanically** — `CodeMySpecLocalWeb.X` → `CodeMySpecWeb.X` is unambiguous and covers 3 of the 9. The remaining 6 anchors still need a real decision.\n\nWhich do you want? And separately worth knowing: 4 source stories point at `component_id`s with no matching component row at all — dangling references in `cli.db` itself, which is why \"97 have a component_id\" but only 93 resolve.", "permission_mode" => "auto", "prompt_id" => "f0c26a41-878e-464d-98eb-d3335cee170c", "session_crons" => [], "session_id" => "80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37", "stop_hook_active" => false, "transcript_path" => "/Users/johndavenport/.claude/projects/-Users-johndavenport-Documents-github-code-my-spec--claude-worktrees-phx-new-generator/80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37.jsonl"}
