[debug] Processing with CmsHarness.Web.HooksController.handle/2
  Parameters: %{"background_tasks" => [], "cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/phx-new-generator", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "6bc4851f-f735-4590-bb1c-c660619b4019", "hook_event_name" => "Stop", "last_assistant_message" => "I can do it from here, and five of the nine are done — `main` at `d8a5d578`.\n\n**Fixed in the source** via `set_story_component` (not SQL — `:4003` holds `cli.db` open, and the tool is the app's own surface):\n\n```\n603, 605, 700  ->  CodeMySpecWeb.AppLive.Overview\n976            ->  CodeMySpecWeb.Tasks.TaskQueueLive\n978            ->  CodeMySpecWeb.AgentProgressLive\n```\n\n**Found a framework bug doing it.** The first call returned `-32603 Tool execution crashed` with no detail. `StoriesMapper.error/1` had clauses for atoms and binaries but not changesets, so any validation failure crashed instead of reporting. There was already a `validation_error/1` that renders changesets — nothing routed to it. Now every caller passing a changeset gets a real message. That fix is committed and covers `main`, though `:4003` runs the released 1.8.2 and won't have it until a release.\n\n**Four still need you.**\n\n**962 \"Per-task help on the agent progress view\"** is blocked, not ambiguous: its `story` narrative is blank, and the changeset requires it — so *no* update to that story can succeed, including one touching only `component_id`. It needs an \"As a… I want… so that…\" written before it can be re-pointed. Arguably the deeper bug is requiring the narrative on an unrelated update, which makes every narrative-less story permanently unupdatable, but I'd rather not loosen validation without your say.\n\n**Three are genuine judgement calls** — the namespace has more than one child and the title doesn't settle it:\n\n- **990** \"Guided intake takes a visitor from an idea to a running app\" → `IntakeLive.Plan` or `IntakeLive.Workspace`? It reads as spanning both.\n- **599** \"Issue Triage\" → `IssuesLive.Index` or `.Show`? I'd guess Index.\n- **560** \"Persona Research\" → `PersonasLive.Index`, `.Show`, or `.FormComponent`? I'd guess Index.\n\nSay the word on those three and I'll finish them, or hand them to whoever owns the story mapping. Once the source is clean, a re-import carries the links across — the migration reads them by module name, and those modules exist at the destination.", "permission_mode" => "auto", "prompt_id" => "cac4b214-ce66-4826-86da-34cdb0d51acb", "session_crons" => [], "session_id" => "80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37", "stop_hook_active" => false, "transcript_path" => "/Users/johndavenport/.claude/projects/-Users-johndavenport-Documents-github-code-my-spec--claude-worktrees-phx-new-generator/80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37.jsonl"}
