  Parameters: %{"background_tasks" => [], "cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/phx-new-generator", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "6bc4851f-f735-4590-bb1c-c660619b4019", "hook_event_name" => "Stop", "last_assistant_message" => "You were right that something else was missing — and it was most of the story.\n\n**The export carried title, narrative, description and status. Nothing else.** Everything else a story holds was silently dropped:\n\n| field | source | destination |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ready_for_dev` | 91 | 1 |\n| `priority` | 52 | 1 |\n| `notes` | 26 | 1 |\n| `specs_ready` | 8 | 0 |\n| `epic_id` | 16 | 0 |\n\n**`ready_for_dev` is why the two views disagree.** It's what releases a story into the requirement graph. Every migrated story arrived parked, so the cloud sees stories the old side doesn't — it isn't that the cloud has *more* unmapped work, it's that 91 ready stories became 0 and the graph has almost nothing it considers live. It looked like a graph problem and was a migration one.\n\n**The epic link is the sharpest case.** `put_stories` has always read `story[\"epic_local_id\"]` to rewire the epic — and `export_story` never wrote that key. So all 16 memberships were dropped while the epics themselves migrated cleanly. A project of empty epics, and the code on both sides looked correct in isolation.\n\nAll of it now travels, and a re-run re-applies it to stories already here — same reasoning as the component links: a first run that predates a field has to be fixable by a second, or a hand-written backfill is the only remedy. Title, narrative and description still don't cross, since those get edited at the destination once a project has moved.\n\nSeven tests, credo clean, `main` at `0563452a`.\n\n**Pull in the main checkout again and I'll re-run it** — that's the third time today, so it's clearly worth automating or at least writing down. Once `:4000` has this, the 99 stories should come back with their readiness, priorities, notes and epics intact, and the graph should finally show you the real picture rather than a parked one.", "permission_mode" => "auto", "prompt_id" => "c956bb9f-d67f-49cb-8d48-fc8655a52d2a", "session_crons" => [], "session_id" => "80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37", "stop_hook_active" => false, "transcript_path" => "/Users/johndavenport/.claude/projects/-Users-johndavenport-Documents-github-code-my-spec--claude-worktrees-phx-new-generator/80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37.jsonl"}
