  Parameters: %{"cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/phx-new-generator", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "6bc4851f-f735-4590-bb1c-c660619b4019", "hook_event_name" => "PreToolUse", "permission_mode" => "auto", "prompt_id" => "e9f40e26-244b-4fb4-9232-f45571a5798d", "session_id" => "80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37", "tool_input" => %{"command" => "elixir -S mix format lib/code_my_spec/migration.ex 2>&1|tail -1; git add lib/code_my_spec/migration.ex && git commit -q -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nCarry every authored field on epics, personas and criteria\n\nAn audit of what each export builds against what each schema holds. Rules\nwere complete; the other three were not.\n\nCriteria lost `kind` — 912 of 921 in this project have one, and none\narrived with it. Kind separates the happy path from the failure path,\nwhich is the shape of a scenario set, so a migrated project looked like\n921 undifferentiated criteria. `verified`/`verified_at` went too; nothing\nis verified here today, so that has cost nothing yet.\n\nEpics lost `slug` and `description`: only the name travelled, so the\ndestination re-derived a slug from the name — a different string whenever\none was edited without the other.\n\nPersonas lost `headline` and `persona_type`, the second of which decides\nwhether a persona is a proto sketch or researched.\n\nEpics and personas also resync on a re-run now, as stories do. Without it\na field added to the export after a project has moved can never reach the\nrows migrated before it, which is exactly why 912 criteria would have sat\nwithout a kind forever.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JPoSfcCJqSqG8iGY9nfyfL\nEOF\n)\" && git log --oneline -1; git fetch origin -q; git merge origin/main --no-edit 2>&1|tail -1; git push origin HEAD:main 2>&1|tail -1", "description" => "Commit and push the field audit fixes", "timeout" => 3000