  Parameters: %{"background_tasks" => [], "cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/phx-new-generator", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "6bc4851f-f735-4590-bb1c-c660619b4019", "hook_event_name" => "Stop", "last_assistant_message" => "You asked for them when the migration was written, and they weren't there. They are now — `main` at `61f8c6c4`.\n\n```\nissues:      149\nquestions:   105\nqa_attempts: 159\n```\n\nVerified by exporting against your real database, not just by tests.\n\n**What was actually wrong:** `export_project/1` built six collections and stopped. The moduledoc said issues and questions travel, so anyone reading it — including me, when I audited — had no reason to doubt it. The docs described the intention and the code never caught up.\n\nThe interesting part was the QA attempts. They reference stories *and* issues, so both id kinds get rewritten against what the run created — an attempt naming an issue by the harness's id would point at nothing at the destination, or worse at another project's row. They export oldest-first and match on `submitted_at` within a story, which is microsecond-precise and right for a point-in-time event. Scenarios needed flattening too: embedded schemas aren't JSON-encodable, so the payload couldn't survive the wire.\n\nIssues match on title within a story and questions on text, so a second run doesn't file all 149 again.\n\n**The full audit, now closed:**\n\n| | status |\n|---|---|\n| stories | all authored fields, incl. readiness, priority, notes, epic |\n| criteria | + `kind` (912 affected), `verified`, `verified_at` |\n| epics | + `slug`, `description` |\n| personas | + `headline`, `persona_type` |\n| rules | complete already |\n| issues / questions / qa_attempts | now migrated |\n\n**To re-run I need the main checkout pulled** — `:4000` is two commits behind and does the importing. Once it's up I'll run it and you'll have the whole project across: readiness, epics, criterion kinds, issue history, questions and the QA audit trail.", "permission_mode" => "auto", "prompt_id" => "96228f9a-5d8c-44d7-bfd1-a718887bf78f", "session_crons" => [], "session_id" => "80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37", "stop_hook_active" => false, "transcript_path" => "/Users/johndavenport/.claude/projects/-Users-johndavenport-Documents-github-code-my-spec--claude-worktrees-phx-new-generator/80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37.jsonl"}
