[debug] Processing with CmsHarness.Web.HooksController.handle/2
  Parameters: %{"background_tasks" => [], "cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/phx-new-generator", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "6bc4851f-f735-4590-bb1c-c660619b4019", "hook_event_name" => "Stop", "last_assistant_message" => "Most of it landed, and two didn't — I've fixed both and pushed at `cf6f3469`.\n\n**Landed:**\n```\nready_for_dev     1 -> 92\nnotes             1 -> 27\npriority          1 -> 53\nquestions         3 -> 108\nissues           87 -> 216\nqa_attempts       0 -> 159\n```\n\n**Didn't:**\n```\nepic links        0 -> 0\ncriteria w/ kind 13 -> 13\n```\n\nBoth for the same reason, and it's the third time this exact shape has caught me. Adding a field to the export only fixes *new* rows — every story and criterion here already exists, so they're recognised and returned untouched, and the field can never reach them. Worse, the summary counted all 99 stories and 921 criteria as carried, so the run *reported* success. That's what makes it quiet rather than obvious.\n\nComponent links, then readiness, now epics and kinds. The lesson I should have generalised two rounds ago: an export change without a matching resync is half a change, and the half that's missing is invisible.\n\n**One more pull and I'll re-run** — that pass should take epic links 0 → 16 and criterion kinds 13 → 912, which is the last of it.", "permission_mode" => "auto", "prompt_id" => "18333283-bce2-4dca-9e77-8daf87f10025", "session_crons" => [], "session_id" => "80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37", "stop_hook_active" => false, "transcript_path" => "/Users/johndavenport/.claude/projects/-Users-johndavenport-Documents-github-code-my-spec--claude-worktrees-phx-new-generator/80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37.jsonl"}
