[debug] Processing with CmsHarness.Web.HooksController.handle/2
  Parameters: %{"background_tasks" => [], "cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/phx-new-generator", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "6bc4851f-f735-4590-bb1c-c660619b4019", "hook_event_name" => "Stop", "last_assistant_message" => "The migration is complete and verified field by field.\n\n**Stories — exact match on every authored field:**\n```\n           source   dest\nstories      99      99\nready        91      91\nepic         16      16\nnotes        26      26\npriority     52      52\n```\n\n**Everything else:**\n```\ncriteria    921  ->  934   (921 migrated + 13 already on story 727)\nrules       547  ->  556   (547 + 9 on 727)\npersonas      4  ->    4\nissues      149  ->  216   (149 + 67 filed at the destination)\nquestions   105  ->  108\nqa_attempts 159  ->  159\n```\n\nCriterion kinds at 925 = the source's 912 plus 727's 13. Component links matched exactly by diff earlier. Nothing is short.\n\n**What it took, and the pattern worth remembering.** Six separate losses, each of which looked like the whole problem when found: the component link was never exported; story ids were reassigned with no way to translate and overlapping ranges, so wrong answers came back confidently; `ready_for_dev`, `priority`, `notes`, `specs_ready` and the epic link were all dropped; criteria lost `kind` on 912 rows; epics and personas lost fields; and issues, questions and QA attempts were never exported at all despite the moduledoc promising two of them.\n\nUnderneath most of those sat one recurring trap: **an export change without a matching resync is invisible.** Existing rows get recognised and returned untouched, the field never reaches them, and the summary still counts them as carried — so the run reports success. It caught me three times, on component links, on readiness, and on epics and kinds. Every reuse path now resyncs.\n\nThe migration is also genuinely idempotent *and* corrective now: re-running writes nothing when nothing changed, and carries upstream fixes when something did. That's what you'll want for prod, where the same class of bug would be much more expensive to find.\n\nWorth noting for prod specifically: `cli.db` is the `prod_cli` store and its token already targets codemyspec.com, so that migration is the single-command form rather than the export/import split we needed here.", "permission_mode" => "auto", "prompt_id" => "c2cdb43b-e793-439b-b667-289fbc446180", "session_crons" => [], "session_id" => "80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37", "stop_hook_active" => false, "transcript_path" => "/Users/johndavenport/.claude/projects/-Users-johndavenport-Documents-github-code-my-spec--claude-worktrees-phx-new-generator/80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37.jsonl"}
